+# Archived court stipulation for the flight telephone exhibits
+
+Public derivative of the November 9, 2026 Eastern source review · TEL02–TEL04 / AUD016-A1. Recovered the complete-looking **16-page public court exhibit ST00004** from two archived court URLs. The PDF bodies match byte for byte. This adds the actual scan and its signature-page evidence to the previous reader-based comparison. The carrier and operator records that support the telephone presentations remain unidentified at item level. [Earlier court-index and reader review](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/3011ef08a684fb9eda16d21cec92474c5bf162d4/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-court-foundation-and-docket-2026-11-09/README.md)
+
+## Archived exhibit and execution fields
+
+The Internet Archive availability replies returned a **May 12, 2009** capture of the historical court path and a **January 30, 2021** capture of the newer court path. Each replay returned a PDF of **593,215 bytes**, SHA-256 `777921360eeea410b21fa5ed0f69c2b1d6cc9b4069cb0b1995b4adf1ec0b7a19`. Preserve both captures and timestamp fields. Their byte identity supports one PDF representation across the two public paths. It gives no independent corroboration of the underlying calls. The live court reader remains a separate representation. [2009 replay](https://web.archive.org/web/20090512234008/http://www.vaed.uscourts.gov/notablecases/moussaoui/exhibits/prosecution/ST00004.pdf) · [2021 replay](https://web.archive.org/web/20210130105845/https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/exhibits/prosecution/ST00004.pdf) · [Current court PDF](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/exhibits/prosecution/ST00004.pdf)
+
+- **Cover.** Physical p. 1 visibly bears `UNDER SEAL` and the Government Exhibit `ST00004` stamp. The court index lists it under Phase 2. The printed title reads `PART II` where local OCR returned `PART I]`. Retain the page-face reading and machine result separately. Keep the face marking, published index and archive access history as distinct observations. The May 2 docket entry **1829** describes an order about selected sealed hearing and bench-conference transcripts. It does not identify this exhibit by number. The exhibit-specific sealing, release and filing chain remains open. [Court exhibit index](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/exhibits/prosecution.html) · [Docket, reader line 110](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/dktsheets/DocketSheet1.html)
+- **Final page and metadata.** Physical p. 16 shows handwritten marks in two separate signing blocks, one for the government and one under `Seen and Agreed` for the defense. The visible blocks carry no separate execution date. The PDF has `D:20060518094721` in its creation-date field. Keep that string, the signing marks and the archive timestamps separate from the unacquired signing and filing dates. The file is an image scan with no extractable default text. The parser returned signature flag `-1` and no embedded files. The handwritten marks are visually observed and have not been authenticated as signatures of particular individuals. [Final page in the archived scan](https://web.archive.org/web/20210130105845/https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/exhibits/prosecution/ST00004.pdf#page=16)
+
+## What the selected clauses cover
+
+| Original clause and exhibit | Checked locator |
+| --- | --- |
+| ¶21 · P200018 · Flight 11 | Physical p. 8, OCR lines 20–23. |
+| ¶22 · P200019 · Flight 175 | Physical pp. 8–9, OCR lines 25–27 and p. 9 line 1. |
+| ¶34 · P200054 · Flight 77 | Physical p. 11, OCR lines 9–12. |
+| ¶36 · P200055 · Flight 93 | Physical p. 11, OCR lines 20–23. |
+| ¶37 · P200056 · Flight 93 recorder presentation | Physical p. 11, OCR lines 25–27. The object of this clause is the exhibit itself. |
+
+The four telephone-related clauses concern the **“underlying documents that support the admission”** of the named presentations. They describe presentations involving crew identification, seating and telephone calls. They supply neither an itemized source list nor field definitions, device identities, operator legs or a source-to-call join. The adjoining recorder clause concerns a different exhibit. The 2016 military-commission transcript labels itself **“UNOFFICIAL/UNAUTHENTICATED”** and preserves an argument pointing to **April 11, 2006, Volume 17A, pp. 3455–3457** for a Flight 93 cockpit-recorder stipulation. The court docket’s candidate session is Volume XVII-A, April 11 at 1:30 p.m., entries **1823** and **1833**. This locator is for the recorder issue raised in that later proceeding. The actual 2006 transcript pages and any telephone-evidence passages remain unacquired. [Court scan, physical pp. 8–11](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/exhibits/prosecution/ST00004.pdf#page=8) · [2016 military transcript, printed p. 12113, lines 2–8](https://www.mc.mil/Portals/0/pdfs/KSM2/KSM%20II%20%28TRANS1June2016-AM2%29.pdf) · [Court docket, reader lines 106 and 122](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/dktsheets/DocketSheet1.html)
+
+Five response hashes, both full PDF bodies, five selected OCR pages and nineteen anchors were checked. The direct military PDF response was HTTP 403. Its selected text was read via the official index. The OCR and visual work is scoped to the reported fields, and signature images and the raw response files are excluded from the public derivative. [Verification and source ledger](SOURCE-PINS.json)
+
+**TODO:** Obtain the signed or filed counterpart with its date and filing or release controls. Locate the actual Volume XVII-A pages and relevant session record for any offer or display of the four telephone presentations. Seek the itemized list behind ST00004 and the actual carrier, operator, office and source-to-exhibit records. Preserve the early connection and later no-connection accounts, differing row counts and duration values at their original scope. The archive finding verifies a stipulation copy and its wording. It supplies no new call-event measurements.
